Integration patch for the Missing Holdings Evidence Investigator (branch agent/missing-holdings-evidence).

The feature commit touches no shared file. This patch is the whole wiring, for the lead to apply:

    git apply backend/api/holdings_evidence/integration.patch

  backend/api/handler.py                          registers POST /evidence/investigate (4 lines)
  infra/template.yaml                             adds the HttpApi event for the route (same authorizer, CORS, throttle as /rules/interpret)
  backend/tests/service/test_service_template.py  the pinned route set: 7 -> 8 routes

No new IAM permission, environment variable or dependency: the route reads the snapshot and policies the API function
already reads, and its optional model wording uses the Bedrock permission and switch the interpreter already has.
Verified with this patch applied: backend/tests + contracts/python/tests all pass.

diff --git a/backend/api/handler.py b/backend/api/handler.py
index ac0650e..57dc3e9 100644
--- a/backend/api/handler.py
+++ b/backend/api/handler.py
@@ -196,6 +196,10 @@ class Api:
             "GET /investigations/{id}": self._get,
             "POST /investigations/{id}/challenge": self._challenge,
         }
+        # Additive, read-only: the Missing Holdings Evidence Investigator (backend/api/holdings_evidence).
+        from backend.api.holdings_evidence.route import ROUTE_KEY as EVIDENCE_ROUTE_KEY, evidence_route
+
+        self._routes[EVIDENCE_ROUTE_KEY] = evidence_route(self)
 
     def handle(self, event: dict[str, Any], context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:
         request_id = (event.get("requestContext") or {}).get("requestId") or getattr(context, "aws_request_id", None)
diff --git a/backend/tests/service/test_service_template.py b/backend/tests/service/test_service_template.py
